\f0\fs24 \cf0 Dear All,\
\
Jose has left for Madrid; he has his own tasks to attend to, though all he has done already is more than enough. He will return on April 30th after the exhibition concludes to take me and the paintings to Fontiveros. He\'92ll remain there with me for the duration of that show.\
\
For the next seven days, I am here in the monastery. A group on a spiritual retreat departed yesterday, leaving me as the sole guest. The cook is kind; when her schedule allows, she prepares wonderful vegetarian meals, and even on her busiest days, the simple dishes she provides are a privilege to receive. The refectory is always stocked with fruit\'97and I must repeat what I said last year: I have never tasted oranges, pears, or peaches as juicy as those here in Spain.\
\
I intend to spend these seven days in quietude. I don\'92t expect to venture out much. Instead, I want to sit in the church and the courtyard, observing the silence and remaining in contemplation. If the writing comes, it comes; I am leaving it to the natural course of things to decide what is required of me while I am here.\
Food is no concern; it is better here than elsewhere. Ordering vegetarian food outside without a Spaniard\'92s help can be a challenge, but I was fortunate to have Jos\'e9 with me while traveling. Now, the meals are at the  monastery.\
\
I hope to have more to share soon. I\'92m receiving various messages from the college, but I find I have little desire to answer. I am only messaging this group; for everything else, I feel I'm unanswerable \uc0\u55357 \u56904 \
\
Warmly,}